    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d470">

                <pb facs="0576" n="508" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg508"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2337½a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        German Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 29, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: The <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi> case is causing me anxiety because of the
                    continued suspension of the negotiation. I am loath to make a formal
                    representation to your Government on the subject, as it might cause you
                    embarrassment, but I feel that the time is very near when I will have to do
                    so.</p>
                <p>I hope, therefore, that you, who appreciate that this state of inaction can not
                    continue much longer, will endeavor to impress your Government with the
                    expediency of reaching a speedy settlement.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
